का॑म m. wish, desire, longing for (gen., dat., or loc.);
love, inclination, lust, pleasure;
 pers. as the god of desire or of
love;
 adj. —˚ (esp. after an inf. stem in तु) wishing for, intending
to. — का॑माय or कामे according to one's wish, out of love for or
for the sake of (gen. or dat.) कामात् & कामतस् voluntarily,
intentionally. कामया (instr. f.) only after ब्रूहि & प्रब्रूहि
freely, unreservedly.

